From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Aug 29 09:16:02 1995
From: "Jose R. Medina Delgado" <jmedina () pupr ! edu>
Date: Tue, 29 Aug 1995 09:16:02 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: <SUMMARY> LAT Problem under OSF-1
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075322406790

My Original problem was trying to disable a port that was already 
defined for LAT . I setup the port with LAT with the following command:

/usr/sbin/latcp -A -p "tty_port" -H "server_name" -R "port_name"

To disable the port what I must type is

/usr/sbin/latcp -D -p "tty_port"

So I can reuse the port with another LAT Server without rebooting the system.

Thanks to jnolan@ibm.net for the response. 

