To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: vdump/vrestore
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075322406543

I am at a loss to understand how to use vdump & vrestore to restore an ADVfs 
fileset to the state it was in at the time of an incremental backup. As far as 
I can make out, restoring from an incremental vdump merely brings back all the 
files that are new or changed since the base dump.  It doesn't redo any delete 
or rename operations that were done since the base dump.

This is very bad news indeed. It is often the case that a great deal more 
intellectual effort goes into the organisation of files than their actual 
contents. I may have spent hours tidying up my filespace, or organising mail 
messages into folders (i.e. directories, with MH).  Having to repeat all that 
work seems to me to defeat the whole purpose of doing incremental dumps.

What I'm looking for is an equivalent of the old "restore" program's "r" 
option. This reinstates structural changes by maintaining a symbol table 
between runs ("restoresymtab").  I believe that it is more or less impossible 
to get it right without such a symbol table.

Please somebody, tell me that I've missed something obvious here...

By the way, the Polycenter Networker product isn't really an option for me, 
even in its "single server" form, since I have to integrate vdump into a 
pre-existing site-wide backup scheme.

Martyn Johnson      maj@cl.cam.ac.uk
University of Cambridge Computer Lab
Cambridge UK

