Here is the question:
> We have a DEC 3000-600 running under OSF/1 v.3.0B and are facing with
> a windows system halt on the console when the machine is loaded with
> four or more background programs. The problem occurs when an eventual
> user logout console with a loaded machine and then it shortly looses
> its windows system, becoming a common terminal. We have overcome the
> problem by renicing background programs to -p 10 but even with this
> measure we sometimes loose console. The question is: Is there a way
> to reactivate the windows system without having to reboot the machine?
  
---------------------

And here comes the prompt reply from Dr. Tom Blinn:

	
/sbin/init.d/xdm stop to stop the X Windows System
/sbin/init.d/xdm start to re-start it.

If it's died, you probably will need to do a stop before you do a start so
that the script can clean up some things (like the record of the pid of the
process that's running xdm) before it will restart things.

